"The Reed Man is real: an Eidhrin Courtier of the Wendle, old, courteous and endlessly hungry."
"He is tall and river-grey, with reed-green hair, gill slits at his throat and eyes like wet slate."
"He cannot lie, and bends every truth he speaks toward a Bargain that feeds him."
"He is far stronger than any Talent in the valley, but can touch only what a Bargain gives him."
"Cold iron, fire and the old words hold him off, and he cannot leave the river's reach."
"He felt the Vestige come through Hollow Tarn and wants it, to Descend among the Courts."
"He has been coming to Lady Varrow's window by the river each night, offering safety for a price."
"His price, once she agrees, is the first Talent that comes to her valley unsworn."
"He will know Nala for what she is the first time she draws Water near running water."
"He would sooner trick Nala into a Bargain than fight her, and fears what Undertow could take."
